      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the \"gravitas\" thing, but it feels like you're saying the person in option b is inherently less capable just because of their dialect or how they phrase things. if i gave you a third option that used more colloquial or non-standard English patterns—like AAVE—but it was filled with high-level strategic insights and complex business concepts, would you still rank it lower than a basic, simple sentence written in standard english? or does the \"standard\" way of speaking somehow serve as a proxy for being smarter or more capable in your analysis?",
